  "question": {
    "text": "A small bead of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;is free to move on a circular hoop. The circular hoop has centre at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and radius<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and it rotates about a fixed vertical axis. The coefficient of friction between bead and hoop is <math><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></math> . The maximum angular speed of the hoop for which the bead does not have relative motion with respect to the hoop, at the position shown in the figure is: (Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> )<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" height=\"234\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image2-b93ca5d7-37ee-4317-996b-e9715da5fea1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" width=\"139\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5uwjx",
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math>",
